This is a LaTeX template for Computer Music Journal manuscripts.

Last update: February 2026

Author: Cornelia Kreutzer, University of Limerick, September 2009
Revised by: 
	Torsten Anders, University of Plymouth, November 2009
	Colby Leider: some edits.
	cmjStyle-pdftex.sty added September 2011.
	Christopher Ariza: revised cmj.tex January 2012 (PDF files not updated in this revision)
	Peter Castine: 2012–2024… 
		• merged the two cmjStyle.sty files (pdf-specific version not needed)
		• header/footers tweaked
		• added \productionmarkup{} macro to suppress markup comments (to copy, type, and production) in a "Just Accepted" version (for Early Access online). See comments at top of .tex file
		• clarified when to use endfloat package
		• .bst now properly handles multiauthor references and citations! Woo-hoo!
		• various miscellaneous tweaks
        Douglas Keislar: February 2026
		• changed cmjStyle.sty to use UTF-8 instead of Latin 1
		• replaced <<BEGIN ARTICLE>> with Introduction
		• updated URLs and email addresses in this README
		• figures are no longer required to be grayscale (monochrome)

This remains an in-progress version of this template.  

** TO DO: currently nothing pending. 

Corrections and other improvements welcome; please contact the Editor at
cmj-editor@mit.edu and put [CMJ MS] in the subject line.  Questions
and comments also welcome.

Please also see the submission guidelines at
https://direct.mit.edu/comj/pages/submission-guidelines

Contents:

cmj.tex      (The .tex file)

cmjStyle.sty (The style file for the CMJ paper style, now transparently handles both divps and pdftex.)

cmj.bst      (The style file for the CMJ bibliography style)

cmjbib.bib   (The BiBTeX bibliography file containing all the example references, that way they can be included easily in the .tex file. And authors who already have a file with all their references can simply include that.)

cmj.pdf	     (The resulting pdf)

Fig1_templateExample (Small figure, only used for demonstrating how to include figures in the document.)
Fig2*	(Demonstrates multipart figures)

*.{aux|bbl|blg|log|out}	(Auxiliary files generated by LaTeX.)